                        "review": "Super Cool Game  that continues the tradition of 'Age of Barbarians' but in shorter more action-packed sequences, \n\n Note it has a 'fighting game' aspect  (like Street Fighter )  and other mini-missions,  it has 2 player combat etc and a variety of characters to choose from.\n\n It has a great art style consistent with the  'Age of Barbarian'  series of games,  -- that 80s and 90s  Lush and Vibrant art style  that makes you feel alive while playing,\n\n Highly recommended for people sick of the modern 'atmospheric' type games that are nothing but trash depression-simulators pretending to be gaming in disguise.\n\n It can be a bit stressful though with the quick deaths  (due to the short nature of the mini-missions)  this isn't about traveling through long journey's like the other Age of Barbarian games",
